description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/patch-with-tools.ts, run the other three deterministic edit checks alongside the vacuous one already there.

WHY. This path self-lands via the mitosis cutover and runs no semantic judge; its recorded verification is "fs_edit applied and typecheck clean". feature_compose runs FOUR checks from the shared module ../vacuous-edit.js - vacuousEditReason, nonTerminatingEditReason, deadStoreEditReason and truncatingRewriteReason - and this file runs only the first. Measured 2026-09-10 against regressions that actually reached origin/dev through this path: truncatingRewriteReason CATCHES 550f2f7, which replaced a refusal function's multi-line body with `return null`, so a refusal returned no refusal and the guard silently stopped guarding. That typechecks perfectly and no compiler can see it. All four are pure functions of (before, after): no model call, no network, no latency, deterministic, so none can false-block under load.

Make exactly ONE edit, and only one. Replace this single line, copied verbatim:

    const vacuousReason = vacuousEditReason(baseContent, afterSrc);

with these lines:

    // ALL FOUR DETERMINISTIC CHECKS, NOT JUST THE FIRST. feature_compose runs the full
    // set from this same module; this path was running one of them. Measured 2026-09-10:
    // truncatingRewriteReason catches 550f2f7, which replaced a refusal function's body
    // with `return null` - a guard that stopped guarding while typechecking cleanly.
    // Imported here rather than at the top so this is a single self-contained change;
    // the region-containment gate above already imports from a sibling this same way.
    const { truncatingRewriteReason, nonTerminatingEditReason, deadStoreEditReason } = await import("../vacuous-edit.js");
    const vacuousReason =
      vacuousEditReason(baseContent, afterSrc) ??
      truncatingRewriteReason(baseContent, afterSrc) ??
      nonTerminatingEditReason(baseContent, afterSrc) ??
      deadStoreEditReason(baseContent, afterSrc);

Do NOT touch the import statement at the top of the file - the dynamic import above makes that unnecessary, and this change must remain a single operation.

Change nothing else. The `if (vacuousReason)` block immediately below, the region-containment gate, the egress gate and the staging code all stay exactly as they are.

SCOPE IS VERIFIED: baseContent and afterSrc are already in scope at this point, the enclosing function resolvePatchWithTools is async so `await import` is valid here, and all four functions share the signature (before: string, after: string) => string | null, so the ?? chain typechecks.

